title: '[asset-hub-westend] Add revive-debug cargo feature for DebugEnabled'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `debug_trace*` RPCs (`debug_traceTransaction`, `debug_traceBlockByNumber`, `debug_traceCall`)
    only work when pallet-revive's `DebugEnabled` config is set to `true`. Currently only the
    dev-node has this enabled, but the dev-node is a simplified environment that doesn't fully
    replicate parachain runtime behavior (e.g. no PoV deduplication). To get accurate debug
    tracing data, it needs to run on actual parachain runtimes.

    This PR adds a `revive-debug` cargo feature to `asset-hub-westend-runtime` so debug mode
    can be toggled at build time without code changes:

    ```bash
    cargo build -p asset-hub-westend-runtime --features revive-debug
    ```

    Other runtimes can adopt the same pattern by adding `revive-debug = []` to their Cargo.toml
    and using `ConstBool<{ cfg!(feature = "revive-debug") }>` for `DebugEnabled`.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
